ion-grade counterexample manuscript by the mixed research pipeline.\",\n    \"The central plan ingests several thousand papers, books, and formal-library artifacts spanning operator algebras, measured group theory, rigidity, group constructions, and relevant invariants.\",\n    \"Formalization covers definitions, dependency graphs, tractable algebraic or combinatorial lemmas, and decisive machine-checkable certificates; completing missing operator-algebra foundations in a proof assistant is primarily represented in the high estimate.\",\n    \"Search cost includes literature acquisition, indexing, embedding, citation traversal, retrieval-model calls, and exploratory database work.\",\n    \"Verification cost includes isolated proof reconstruction, adversarial critic passes, computational replication, consistency checks on hypotheses, theorem-prover work, and preparation of verifier reports.\",\n    \"Total costs include model inference, orchestration, storage, retrieval, specialized computation, failed branches, formalization, replication, and manuscript production, but exclude journal review time and salaries for external human mathematicians.\",\n    \"Parallel execution is assumed, so elapsed hours are wall-clock hours rather than summed agent-hours.\",\n    \"Because the lane is non-governed, no cost is assigned to identity hashing, cryptographic branch receipts, enforced budgets, evidence-preservation policy, or policy checks; publication-grade verification remains included separately.\"\n  ],\n  \"uncertainty_drivers\": [\n    \"Ambiguity in the exact formulation and scope of the conjecture, including which group class and notion of uniqueness must be refuted.\",\n    \"The length, novelty, and prerequisite depth of the construction and its von Neumann algebra analysis.\",\n    \"Whether the decisive argument depends on techniques poorly represented in model training data or inaccessible literature.\",\n    \"Difficulty detecting subtle failures of group hypotheses, factoriality assumptions, trace preservation, or the claimed algebra isomorphism.\",\n    \"Large proof-assistant library gaps for advanced von Neumann algebra and rigidity theory.\",\n    \"Risk that exploratory agents repeatedly rediscover nearby examples that fail one essential hypothesis.\",\n    \"Long-horizon coherence limitations across thousands of definitions, citations, and interacting lemmas.\",\n    \"Contamination of the nominally independent track by memorized or indirectly retrieved details of the published construction.\",\n    \"Unknown effectiveness of computational experiments in a problem whose decisive steps may be predominantly conceptual.\",\n    \"API pricing, context-window limits, model availability, and the amount of parallel inference required for reliable critic diversity.\"\n  ],\n  \"minimum_evidence\": [\n    \"A precise, citation-supported statement of the conjecture and all hypotheses being negated.\",\n    \"Explicit descriptions of the candidate groups and proofs that each belongs to the required class.\",\n    \"A complete proof that the groups are non-isomorphic, preferably using at least two independently checked invariants or arguments where available.\",\n    \"A complete construction and verification of the asserted isomorphism between the associated von Neumann algebras, including trace, factoriality, and completion issues.\",\n    \"A dependency-complete proof reconstruction in which every nonstandard external theorem is stated with verified hypotheses and a stable source.\",\n    \"At least two isolated verifier-agent reconstructions that do not share intermediate summaries with the primary derivation agents.\",\n    \"Adversarial searches for collapsed distinctions, hidden conjugacies, missing hypotheses, circular citations, and stronger or weaker equivalence notions.\",\n    \"Reproducible code, data, and machine-checkable certificates for every computational claim.\",\n    \"Formalized definitions and decisive tractable lemmas, plus an explicit audit trail for analytic steps beyond current proof-assistant libraries.\",\n    \"A replication package and manuscript whose central argument can be reconstructed from preserved sources and artifacts without relying on hidden model reasoning.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"Failure to pin down a single authoritative formulation of the conjecture and target group class.\",\n    \"Absence of machine-readable formal foundations for the required operator-algebraic machinery.\",\n    \"Inability of model critics to reliably identify subtle gaps in advanced analytic and rigidity arguments.\",\n    \"A construction whose key insight is not reachable through scalable enumeration, analogy, or computational experimentation.\",\n    \"Unresolvable uncertainty about whether an allegedly independent derivation was contaminated by the known result.\",\n    \"Context and memory limits that prevent globally consistent management of a very large proof dependency graph.\",\n    \"Insufficiently diverse independent verifier models, causing correlated proof errors.\",\n    \"Licensing or access restrictions on essential literature.\",\n    \"Need for new foundational lemmas whose proof burden exceeds the allocated high-case budget and time.\"\n  ]\n}"
